  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Voices for Climate Action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Voices for Climate Action in Shinyanga is a twelve-month project focusing on empowering youth to participate in and drive innovative initiatives addressing the pressing climate challenges facing the community by driving accountability and responsiveness from the government. The project will strengthen meaningful youth engagement in decision-making bodies related to climate change adaptation and mitigation and improve the level of accountability and commitment of local government decision-makers in responding to youth voices on climate change action. The project is expected to increase the representation and participation of youth in climate decision-making structures at local and national levels, enhance the capacity of youth to advocate for and implement climate policies and initiatives and increase government accountability in addressing climate impacts and responding to youth demands. The project aimsto engage and directly reach 5,000 youth from diverse backgrounds, with at least 50% of them being women and 10% representing people with disabilities. These rights holders will benefit from capacity-building workshops, leadership training, and opportunities to participate in climate policy advocacy and decision-making platforms</narrative>
  </description>
