  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth and Women Emancipation (YAWE) is a youth-led innovative development organization focusing on empowering the poorest women, youth, and children in Tanzania. YAWE is registered under the Tanzania NGO Act No. 24 of 2002 and is legally mandated to operate in Tanzania Mainland. Our organization&apos;s objective is to enhance sustainable development, promote equality, and address systemic challenges. We envision a society in which empowered and responsible youth, children, and women make informed decisions about their health and lives. Our mission is to contribute towards sustainable and inclusive development in Tanzania through education, mentorship, and innovative programs designed to improve the well-being of youth, children, and women. YAWE is for everyone who believes in our five core values: transparency, accountability, professionalism, partnership, and non-discrimination. YAWE is governed by the Annual General Meeting (AGM), which is the highest decision-making body of the organization. The AGM has delegated its mandate to the Board of Directors, which is composed of five members. The organization&apos;s daily activities and operations are managed by the Executive Director, who is also the secretary of the Board of Directors and is accountable to them. Under the Executive Director, there is a management team, which consists of the technical heads of departments, including the Programs Manager, MEAL Manager, Finance and Administration Manager, and Business and Development Manager. This chain of command extends down to other supporting staff members, who reportto their respective line managers.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth and Women Emancipation</narrative>
